\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. 'Tis not to ask for gifts alone,
\par I kneel in prayer before His throne;
\par But, seeking fellowship divine,
\par I feel His love, and know it mine.
\par When I can pray.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. 'Tis prayer that makes my spirit strong
\par To do the right and fear the wrong,
\par To know the peace of sins forgiven,
\par To breathe the atmosphere of heaven;
\par To live, I pray.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I ought to pray, because my voice
\par Can make the Father's heart rejoice;
\par He loves His child, and He will meet
\par And hold communication sweet
\par With one who prays.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Therefore I seek my God, and raise
\par My grateful thanks, my fervent praise;
\par While evil passions and deceit
\par Will vanish when before His feet
\par I kneel to pray.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. And if, great Father, when I pray,
\par Thy answer can be only \tab Nay,
\par Still Thou wilt comfort me and bless
\par With visions of Thy righteousness:
\par Help me to pray
\par \cf1\ul\b  \f1\fs16 
\par 
\par }

